window.docContents[241].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.GenericGame/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___GenericGame":{"contents":"Paper › Computational/Specifications/Game › GenericGame.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 1 headline theorem depend on it 94 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\n\n\nGeneric multi-session composed security game G(Σ)Trusted: the statement. Read with Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementBinaryHarnessCore.lean, which defines the shared oracle signatures, KeyInd state, and end-of-game freshness predicate. See Computational/docs/TRUSTED_BASE.md.Models the generic multi-session composed game G(Σ) (§4.2, docs/PAPER_MAP.md) as an experiment composedExp I A over a protocol interface I : ComposedIface S ℓ. The adversary interacts with PQXDH handshakes, promotes handshake sessions via startDR, and attacks promoted instances as ACD19 secure-messaging (SM.spec) sessions. Two interfaces instantiate ComposedIface: the CLI interface cliIface (Σ_bin in Computational/Specifications/Game/StatementPq.lean, fixed to the binary-harness handshake bhDrvKeyInd) and the model interface modelIface (Σ_model^H in Computational/Specifications/Game/ModelIface.lean, parameterized by a KeyInd handler H).Independently of I, composedExp samples one challenge bit b shared across all promoted ratchet instances, initializes KeyIndState.empty S true so startDR promotes real handshake keys, checks allTestedSessionsFresh I.prims on the separate KeyIndState layer at the end of the run (returning a uniform coin on failure), and otherwise wins on b' == b || I.won d b. That I uses b solely for challenge queries is a property of each concrete ComposedIface, and query budgets are imposed as theorem hypotheses.\n\n\n\ndef composedDrSpecL51–55 ↗#Per-instance secure-messaging oracle family of G(Σ) with leaked-state type St, indexed by instance number (cliGameDrSpec ℓ (BitVec 512) at St = BinState).\n\nabbrev composedSpecL57–60 ↗#Full adversary oracle signature in G(Σ): uniform coins, KeyInd, startDR, and per-instance secure-messaging oracles (cliGameSpec S ℓ (BitVec 512) at St = BinState).\n\nstructure ComposedIfaceL62–76 ↗#Protocol interface Σ instantiating the composed game G(Σ).\n\ndef composedExpL78–87 ↗#Composed security experiment G(Σ): runs A against I.impl b from I.init b and KeyIndState.empty S true for uniform b, and returns a uniform coin if allTestedSessionsFresh fails or b' == b || I.won d b otherwise.\n\ndef ComposedAdvantageL89–95 ↗#Distinguishing advantage 2 |Pr[composedExp I A = true] - 1/2| of A in G(Σ).\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"Computational/Specifications/Game/GenericGame.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/Computational.Specifications.Game.GenericGame/#file-Computational___Specifications___Game___GenericGame"}});